			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Update Element submodule to enforce telemetry defaults and fix native startup\n\nSynchronize the Element submodule to commit ac14a2e4, incorporating critical stability fixes and privacy-by-default telemetry policies across the core component stack.\n\nKey modifications:\n\n**Telemetry Policy:**\nShift default values for `Report`, `Capture`, and `OTLPEnabled` to `false` in Common and Sky. Mountain retains `true` for development diagnostics but enforces strict runtime consent gates in the `bootstrap-fork.js` sidecar.\n\n**Native Backend Fixes:**\nAddress a critical startup blocker in Mountain by explicitly initializing the native keyring store (`keyring::use_native_store`) to resolve 'No default store has been set' errors affecting extensions like Roo Code.\n\n**Build & Platform:**\nUpdate Maintain to inject runtime environment variables into `Info.plist` via a new `PlistEdit` module. Patch Output to enforce polling-based `DOMContentLoaded` fallbacks, resolving WebKit Tauri deadlocks. Standardize `Terminal` and `GPU` directory casing and rebuild Cocoon artifacts to reflect updated route manifests.\n\nThese changes stabilize the native backend lifecycle, secure the telemetry pipeline, and resolve platform-specific webview hangs.",
			"SHA": "8e438e8d71065b6aad079f933232e7d2218016b3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T16:17:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Update submodules and standardize gRPC casing\n\nSynchronize the Dependency and Element submodules to incorporate upstream VS Code stability improvements for the Agents window and SSH remote handling, alongside internal architectural refinements.\n\nKey modifications:\n\n**Dependency (VS Code):**\nUpdate upstream to e94b4c4. This sync resolves terminal lifecycle issues in the Agents window, implements SSH keyboard-interactive authentication fallback, and adds a watchdog for dead TCP transports. Note: The setting `extensions.supportSessionsWindow` is renamed to `extensions.supportAgentsWindow`.\n\n**Element (Land Components):**\nUpdate to 9f05dcc5 to fix Mountain compile errors and enhance SecretProvider error handling. Standardize gRPC naming conventions across Cocoon, Wind, and Air by changing \"GRPC\" to \"gRPC\" to align with architectural naming standards. Regenerate interface definitions and apply dependency security patches across Sky, Worker, and Output.\n\n**Configuration:**\nCorrect the casing of `TierRemoteProcedureCall` from \"GRPC\" to \"gRPC\" in `.env.Land.Sample` to match the updated type values in the Element codebase.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: The setting `extensions.supportSessionsWindow` has been renamed to `extensions.supportAgentsWindow`.",
			"SHA": "86812020dd5cbe97a7ab98286294fe5fadbcdbec"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-12T00:09:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to 9d1c3a62\n\nUpdate the Element submodule reference to the latest upstream commit 9d1c3a62, bringing in continued maintenance improvements and upstream synchronization across the Land editor component stack.\n\nThis routine submodule update ensures the Land workspace incorporates the latest Element changes from the shared git tree.",
			"SHA": "647932539422480ceddd26601fbaf9739294a386"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-11T22:37:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Land): Pin Tauri ecosystem versions and enforce nightly Rust toolchain\n\nRestructure the workspace dependency management to use explicit version pinning (=) for all Tauri-related crates in both the workspace.dependencies table and [patch.crates-io] section. Previously, plugins like tauri-plugin-dialog and tauri-plugin-fs had floating versions that could drift. Now every tauri-*, wry, tao, muda, and tray-icon crate uses exact version pinning to ensure reproducible builds across CI and developer machines.\n\nKey changes:\n\n**Cargo.toml dependency management:**\n- Add pinned (=) versions to all existing workspace.dependencies and patch entries\n- Remove Dependency/Tauri from the exclude list (unnecessary with proper patching)\n- Add all 18 Tauri plugins not previously listed (autostart, clipboard-manager, http, notification, shell, etc.)\n- Add standalone ecosystem crates: wry, tao, muda, tray-icon, window-vibrancy, window-shadows, global-hotkey\n- Add tauri-cli, tauri-bundler, tauri-driver, tauri-macos-sign for build tooling\n- Bump OXC crates (0.128.0 → 0.129.0), tonic (0.14.5 → 0.14.6), tokio (1.52.1 → 1.52.3), opentelemetry (0.31.0 → 0.32.0), and other transitive dependencies\n\n**.cargo/config.toml release profile:**\n- Set release opt-level to 3 (was 2 to avoid OXC bugs, now fixed)\n- Remove platform-specific rustflags for aarch64 and x86_64 darwin targets\n\n**rust-toolchain.toml:**\n- Introduce explicit nightly toolchain requirement with rustfmt and clippy components\n- Define dev (opt-level 0) and release (opt-level 3) profiles\n- This replaces the previous implicit stable toolchain\n\n**package.json dev dependencies:**\n- Update @biomejs/biome (2.4.12 → 2.4.15), @playform/build (0.3.1 → 0.3.2), turbo (2.9.6 → 2.9.12)\n- Bump prettier-plugin-svelte, prettier-plugin-tailwindcss, prettier-plugin-ember-template-tag\n\nSubmodule syncs bring Mountain error handling improvements, OXC compatibility fixes, and upstream VS Code 7c59d899 with Agents window support.",
			"SHA": "3a1c89ddc6a5a2a859bb75dac182923d205a9507"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-09T17:54:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				115,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Sky): Configure TypeScript lib and module resolution settings\n\nUpdate `tsconfig.json` and `jsconfig.json` in the Sky editor UI component layer to explicitly define the compilation environment. Add `ESNext`, `DOM`, and `DOM.Iterable` to the `lib` array to ensure proper type checking for modern browser APIs used in the Astro/React frontend. Set `ignoreDeprecations` to \"6.0\" to align with the current TypeScript target.\n\nReorder `extends` to the bottom of `tsconfig.json` to allow local `compilerOptions` like `moduleResolution: \"Bundler\"` and `module: \"esnext\"` to take precedence over the base `@playform/build` configuration.\n\nThis ensures consistent type resolution across the Sky component tree and prevents implicit `any` errors related to missing DOM definitions.",
			"SHA": "b7bd3eb59ee0a5d9a6f59f9c28884f6acdd6fe9f"
		}
	],
